  "prompt": "Create one NEW advanced benefit test CASE as JSON matching the schema. Use only synthetic supplied facts, integer cents, exact fields, and no assumptions. Every successful step requires ALL observable fields. Submit success is 201, others 200. Calculate independent expected values, ledger amounts/counts, history/revision and member/family accumulators. Use a fresh case state. submit data has claim_id (not id), operation_key, member_id, plan_id, service_date, lines. pay/reverse/adjust/appeal/resolve data has claim_id,operation_key,expected_revision, and note where schema requires. Use unique operation keys except intentional identical replay. Allowed claim/line IDs have at least 3 characters. The first submit is revision 1/event count 1. Finance pays; adjuster adjusts/resolves; owner appeals. Other payer applies before deductible. Cap member charge at OOP. Annual benefit excess is noncovered. After adjustment retain paid state and add TWO ledger entries (credit old, debit new); reversal adds one credit. Appeal adds history without repricing; resolution reprices and returns adjudicated. After rejected writes on existing claims add an authorized unchanged-state readback. Do not call tools, generate code, invent endpoints or auto-approve. Maximum 6 steps for this request.\nREQUIREMENT: Use commercial_ppo, M100, 2026-03-01. Submit a 100000-cent medical claim, pay it, adjust it to 50000 cents, then reverse and read back restored ledger and accumulators. At most six steps. Produce one case.\nFACTS: {\"actors\": {\"adjuster-demo\": {\"id\": \"adjuster-demo\", \"label\": \"Adjuster / demo\", \"member_id\": null, \"role\": \"adjuster\"}, \"auditor-demo\": {\"id\": \"auditor-demo\", \"label\": \"Auditor / read only\", \"member_id\": null, \"role\": \"auditor\"}, \"customer-m100\": {\"id\": \"customer-m100\", \"label\": \"Customer / M100\", \"member_id\": \"M100\", \"role\": \"customer\"}, \"customer-m200\": {\"id\": \"customer-m200\", \"label\": \"Customer / M200\